From 995088a5729bac31c95b1921d344f36563f2a272 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: yinvoker <yinvoker@outlook.com>
Date: Thu, 3 Sep 2026 16:01:45 +0800
Subject: [PATCH] patch: SMMLA (Armv8.6 i8mm) int8 GEMM path, runtime-gated,
 ruy fallback

On CPUs that report HWCAP2_I8MM (Armv9 cores: Cortex-X2/X4, A710/A720,
A510/A520) Multiply8Rui now runs an in-tree SMMLA kernel
(tensors/cpu/smmla_gemm.cpp); every other CPU keeps the ruy SDOT path
unchanged. Same integer math, so accumulators are bit-identical -- the
canonical corpus hashes are unchanged on 8 Gen 3, 8 Gen 1, 865 and the
M3 host, on both paths. BERGAMOT_NO_I8MM=1 forces the ruy path for
same-binary A/B and diagnostics.

Kernel: pair-interleaved packing (row/col pairs x 8-deep octets),
8x8 tile with 16 register accumulators plus 4x8 / 2x8 tiles for
decode-tail M and a guarded edge tile; weights prepacked per thread
under the same generation guard as the ruy prepacked cache (0011);
shortlist-selected B packed per call like ruy does. The TU alone is
compiled with -march=armv8.2-a+dotprod+i8mm; the i8mm opcodes must
stay confined to it (tools/smmla-test/check-opcodes.sh enforces).

Measured (same binary, interleaved, same frequency caps): 8 Gen 3
single sentence 1.35x, w2 1.23x, blocking 1.16x, pivot 1.15x;
8 Gen 1 single sentence 1.37x, blocking 1.26x, pivot 1.27x, w2 1.23x;
865 (no i8mm) fallback 3360 vs 3361 ms. Host M3 is -3..-5% (Apple cores
issue sdot and smmla at the same rate) and is not the judge.

Test set, hash regression and device list: tools/smmla-test,
tools/regress-hash.sh, docs/smmla-compatibility.md.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Fable 5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
